{"name":"Arctic Dusk","hex":"#816678","fetched":"2026-10-11","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"arctic","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Adjective","definitions":["Alternative letter-case form of Arctic."]},{"part":"Proper noun","definitions":["Alternative letter-case form of Arctic."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/arctic"},{"term":"dusk","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Adjective","definitions":["Tending to darkness or blackness; moderately dark or black; dusky."]},{"part":"Noun","definitions":["The time after the sun has set but when the sky is still lit by sunlight; the evening twilight period.","A darkish colour."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/dusk"}],"entries":[{"title":"Arctic","blocks":[{"text":"The Arctic is the polar region of Earth that surrounds the North Pole, lying north of the Arctic Circle. The Arctic region, from the IERS Reference Meridian travelling east, consists of parts of northern Norway, northernmost Sweden, northern Finland, Russia, the United States (Alaska), Canada, Danish Realm (Greenland), and northern Iceland, along with the Arctic Ocean and adjacent seas."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/f/f0/Arctic_%28orthographic_projection_with_highlights%29.svg/330px-Arctic_%28orthographic_projection_with_highlights%29.svg.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Arctic","wikidata":"Q25322"},{"title":"Dusk","blocks":[{"text":"Dusk occurs at the darkest stage of twilight, or at the very end of astronomical twilight after sunset and just before nightfall. At predusk, during early to intermediate stages of twilight, enough light in the sky under clear conditions may occur to read outdoors without artificial illumination; however, at the end of civil twilight, such lighting is required to read outside. The term dusk usually refers to astronomical dusk, or the darkest part of twilight before night begins."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/1/1f/Landers_in_the_Mojave_Desert_at_dusk%2C_looking_west_from_Joshua_Tree%2C_California_USA.jpg/330px-Landers_in_the_Mojave_Desert_at_dusk%2C_looking_west_from_Joshua_Tree%2C_California_USA.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Dusk","wikidata":"Q11288132"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/8/8f/Arctica_surface.jpg/500px-Arctica_surface.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/8/8f/Arctica_surface.jpg/500px-Arctica_surface.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3AArctica_surface.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/5/5c/Sunny_Skies_over_the_Arctic_in_Late_June_2010.jpg/500px-Sunny_Skies_over_the_Arctic_in_Late_June_2010.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/5/5c/Sunny_Skies_over_the_Arctic_in_Late_June_2010.jpg/1280px-Sunny_Skies_over_the_Arctic_in_Late_June_2010.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/5/5c/Sunny_Skies_over_the_Arctic_in_Late_June_2010.jpg/500px-Sunny_Skies_over_the_Arctic_in_Late_June_2010.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3ASunny_Skies_over_the_Arctic_in_Late_June_2010.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/2/22/Aerial_photograph_Greenland_2023-10-14-3.jpg/500px-Aerial_photograph_Greenland_2023-10-14-3.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/2/22/Aerial_photograph_Greenland_2023-10-14-3.jpg/1280px-